<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mat (river)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mati</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mat is a river in north-central Albania, about 115 kilometres long, flowing west through a mountainous valley to the Adriatic north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezhe">Lezhë</a>. The surrounding district, also called Mat, was a stronghold of clans and noble families such as the Kastrioti in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. In the 20th century it was the home region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Ahmet Zogu</a>, later King Zog I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mat-river.jpg" alt="Mat (river)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albinfo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mat_Unterlauf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
